// The post-quantum recipient type: MLKEM768-X25519, the hybrid X-Wing KEM under
// HPKE.
//
// https://c2sp.org/age (the mlkem768x25519 stanza)
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9180 (HPKE)
//
// A file sealed to this type stays sealed against an adversary who can run
// Shor's algorithm, because opening it needs both an ML-KEM-768 secret and an
// X25519 one. The two are combined into a single secret rather than negotiated,
// so breaking either alone leaves nothing to attack.
//
// A recipient is an ML-KEM encapsulation key followed by an X25519 public key,
// 1216 bytes, written as `age1pq1…`; a secret is one thirty-two-byte seed,
// written as `AGE-SECRET-KEY-PQ-1…`. The seed is expanded into both halves,
// which is why one short string is the whole of an identity.
//
// The format treats this type as one that should not share a file with the
// others: sealing to a post-quantum recipient and an X25519 one at once gives a
// file only as strong as the weaker of the two. This library leaves that rule to
// the caller — the header carries both, and a reader opens whichever stanza is
// its own — but a sender with nothing else in mind should address a file to
// post-quantum recipients alone.
//
// Not here: where the seed is stored. It is thirty-two bytes, and keeping it is
// the caller's business.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonbase/base64",
  "moonbitstack/moonseal/internal/keytext",
  "moonbitstack/moonseal/internal/hpke",
  "moonbitstack/moonseal/spec",
  "moonbitstack/moonseed",
}

import {
  "moonbitstack/moonseal",
  "moonbitstack/moonseal/spec",
  "moonbitstack/moonseed",
} for "test"
